{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "HTML Javascript"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about scripts."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macrosystem processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs with Infinitives: Have to in Affirmative Statements and Yes No Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p style=\"text-align:justify\">In English, there are many verbs that demand the following action to be in infinitive form. <span class=\"strong\">To Have</span> is one of those verbs that demand the action to be in infinitive form.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We in present can use <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> tense and interrogative form to express necessity, obligation and certainty.</br></br>  Use the following structure to make a sentence with have to. </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"Subject + <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> + <span class=\"strong\">base form of verb</span> + complement. </div></br></br>  Example: </br>  <ul>\t<li><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to implement</span> JavaScript to create script lines into html.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">The browser <span class=\"strong\">has to have</span> the script options activated to display the web app. </span></li></br></br> </ul>  Note that the conjugation of have to in third person singular is <span class=\"strong\">has to</span>.</br>  Use the following structure to make close-ended (yes/no) questions with have to. </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"<span class=\"strong\">Do/Does</span> + Subject + <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> + <span class=\"strong\">main verb base form</span> + complement + ? </div></br>  <ul> <li><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Do</span> I <span class=\"strong\">have to work</span> with Java and JavaScript to create web apps?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Does</span> the app <span class=\"strong\">have to allow</span> scripts to work? </span></li> </ul></br>  Notice that you use the auxiliary do to make questions with have."}, {"type": "example", "content": "if you want to change or modify aspects of your webpage, you have to use script language."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you need to call an event like a pop up when the mouse is over an element, you have to implement an event handler."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "VBScript"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a script language based on Visual Basic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The most common script languages that we can use are JavaScript and VBScript."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "JavaScript"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a script language programmers use in web design to implement scripts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I know that by know, you all have to be a little confused with the use of JavaScript and HTML, but indeed, they are really easy to understand."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drop-down box"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a menu that lists a set of choices when you click on it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's imagine you have to create a drop-down box that allows you to edit the content or aspect of a box, image, or text."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "display"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show on a screen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to remember that not all browsers allow scripts because they are blocked or the browser is too old to display them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "issue"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a problem"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to insert the nonscript element in your HTML code to alert the user of that issue\u2026"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for the events that can trigger your script. Make a list."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 3 events and think about uses that you could give them in a website."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your ideas with a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can identify and list different events to trigger scripts in HTML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can interpret and give examples of some events for HTML scripts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can discuss different uses for scripts in HTML."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Commands for Different Types of HTML Scripts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "HTML and JavaScript commonly work together within a website to provide the user more interactivity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align:justify\">As you probably know, HTML is the base that programmers use to display webpages, but unfortunately, it is the only property HTML has. Therefore, what really provides interactivity between the user and the website is JavaScript.</br></br>  JavaScript is a programming language based on Java that allows the programmers to make a webpage dynamic, that is, to change the values of an HTML tag by interacting with the webpage everytime the user clicks on a drop-down box or a button. </br></br>  Depending on how you design your website you can make use of many of the script commands that can allow you to insert scripts into your HTML text. </br></br>  Let's check in the following chart some of the most common script types that are there in HTML-based pages. </p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Script</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Description</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"External JavaScript\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You create the script commands in a separate file with the extension <span class=\\\"strong\\\">.js</span> to use the scripts in different HTML files.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Internal JavaScript\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You generate the script code in any part of your HTML document inside a script tag (<span class=\\\"strong\\\">< script text >< /script ></span>)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Event handlers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An event handler script is a command that allows an action to take place after you click or move the mouse.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hide scripts \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"As some browsers do not accept or support scripts, you can protect the script and hide it from users between HTML commands. Example: < <span class=\\\"strong\\\">script type= </span>\u201ctext/javascript\u201d >\u2026< /<span class=\\\"strong\\\">script</span> >\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"< nonscript > Elements\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can use the HTML command < nonscipt</span> >\u2026< /<span class=\\\"strong\\\">nonscript </span>> to warn the users that their browser does not accept or allow scripts.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: I know that by know, you all have to be a little confused with the use of JavaScript and HTML, but indeed, they are really easy to understand. Let's imagine that by means of HTML commands and string codes, you display the content of your website, but just that. You can't make it interactive. I mean, you can't change anything from what is there. But, if you want to change or modify aspects of your webpage, you have to use script language. </br><span class=\"strong\">Dakota</span>: Sorry, teacher. But, what's a script?"}, {"time": "35000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: Ok\u2026 to answer that question, let's imagine you have to create a drop-down box that allows you to edit the content or aspect of a box, image, or text that your HTML code displays on the website. To do so, you have to add some extra codes that for obvious reason differ from the common HTML codes, you have to write those codes in script language. The most common script languages that we can use are JavaScript and VBScript. Is that clear now? </br><span class=\"strong\">Dakota</span>: Yes, sir. But, could you give some examples about it?"}, {"time": "71000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: Sure, some important scripts that you have to know by hart are, the internal and external JavaScript's ones, the event handlers and the nonscript elements. </br><span class=\"strong\">Dakota</span>: How do they work? </br><span class=\"strong\">Miguel</span>: That's an excellent question, if you want to write a script in different HTML documents, you have to use the external one, but if you only want to write the script in one webpage, you have to use the internal one. If you need to call an event like a pop up when the mouse is over an element, you have to implement an event handler. Now, you have to remember that not all browsers allow scripts because they are blocked or the browser is too old to display them; in those cases, you have to insert the nonscript element in your HTML code to alert the user of that issue\u2026"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the concept of script in HTML. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can list different types of scripts in HTML. "}, {"